course: dictionary
lesson: 9486
title: Name clues and context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A steamboat is a boat driven by a steam engine. Its name gives you two clues: steam and boat. Put the clues together and you can often guess a new word.
explain: Context clues help too. Words like rivers, paddle wheel and 1800s tell you the steamboat was an old boat that travelled on rivers, not a modern ship on the sea.
explain: Sometimes a word is part of a name. In «Steamboat Willie», the word is the title of a cartoon. Here the clue is the words around it: a cartoon is a film, so Steamboat Willie is a film title, not a boat you could ride on.
fact: A steamboat is a boat driven by a steam engine.
fact: Many steamboats had a large paddle wheel that pushed the boat through the water.
fact: Steamboats carried people and goods up and down rivers such as the Mississippi, especially in the 1800s.
fact: «Steamboat Willie» is a cartoon from 1928, the first Mickey Mouse cartoon with sound.
fact: Some steamboats still run today, carrying tourists.
exercise: What is a steamboat? | A car that runs on coal | A boat with sails made of cloth | *A boat driven by a steam engine | A train that travels under water
exercise: Steamboats carried goods up and down which river? | Nile | *Mississippi | Thames | Amazon
exercise: «The old steamboat turned its huge paddle wheel and chugged along the river.» What does the paddle wheel most likely do? | Holds the sails up | Makes the boat sing | *Pushes the boat through the water | Keeps the boat in the air
test: Steamboats were common on rivers in the 1800s. What time period does this show? | The 1400s | The 2000s | *The 1800s | The 1900s
test: In «Steamboat Willie», what is the word part of? | A museum | A recipe book | *A cartoon film | A football match
exam: Using the clues in its name, what would a steamboat most likely be? | A bicycle that floats on water | A fish that swims very fast | A boat powered by batteries | *A boat powered by steam
